### Function 2: Requires + &mut

```xiom
fn prepend(items: &mut Vec[Int], value: Int)
  ensures: items.len() == items@pre.len() + 1;
  ensures: items[0] == value;
{
  // Insert value at the front
  items.push(value);
  let i = items.len() - 1;
  while i > 0 {
    let temp = items[i];
    items[i] = items[i - 1];
    items[i - 1] = temp;
    i = i - 1;
  }
}
```

### Function 3: All Four

```xiom
fn safe_transfer(from: &mut Account, to: &mut Account, amount: Float64)
  requires: amount > 0.0;
  requires: from.balance >= amount;
  ensures: from.balance == from@pre.balance - amount;
  ensures: to.balance == to@pre.balance + amount;
  ensures: from.balance >= 0.0;
{
  from.balance = from.balance - amount;
  to.balance = to.balance + amount;
}
```

### The Complete Safety Stack

| Layer | Mechanism | What It Prevents |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| Logic | requires | Invalid inputs |
| Logic | ensures | Wrong outputs |
| Type | invariant | Invalid states |
| Memory | & | Use-after-free |
| Memory | &mut | Data races |
| Memory | move | Double-free |

